2026-09-27T07:55:12.7619797Z Description:
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7620380Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7620844Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7621994Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7623456Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7623630Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7623970Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7624471Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7624964Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7668096Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7668630Z ================
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7668976Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7669437Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7669993Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7670322Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7670535Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7670977Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7671254Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7671456Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7672064Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7672591Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7673577Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7674384Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7674540Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7675152Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7675926Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7676326Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7676763Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7677569Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7677691Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7677966Z ========
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7678132Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7680070Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7682109Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7682438Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7683120Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7684201Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7685053Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7685882Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7769450Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7770365Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7770545Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7770960Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7771230Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7772943Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7774763Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7775740Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7777269Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:55:12.7777600Z 
